                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "afc9fb67-faa2-3a90-af70-79ea6c61d8a3",
                                        "entry_id": "7012547b-5700-3c3c-929b-7175e01cf81e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who solicits."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af7e728b-8748-4699-b6bc-c38a1b7600f2",
                                                "sense_id": "afc9fb67-faa2-3a90-af70-79ea6c61d8a3",
                                                "text": "“I beg, Mr Allworthy,” answered Sophia, “you will not insist on my reasons;—[…] Your nephew, sir, hath many virtues—he hath great virtues, Mr Allworthy. I question not but he will do you honour in the world, and make you happy.”—“I wish I could make him so, madam,” replied Allworthy; “but that I am convinced is only in your power. It is that conviction which hath made me so earnest a solicitor in his favour.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c1b9e38-21f1-444e-95fa-c378f41f89d6",
                                                "sense_id": "afc9fb67-faa2-3a90-af70-79ea6c61d8a3",
                                                "text": "[…] sex workers are regarded as born to be punished; the solicitors of their services are not."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bbabd753-ba16-3146-ac2c-8400d6effe04",
                                        "entry_id": "7012547b-5700-3c3c-929b-7175e01cf81e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In many common law jurisdictions, a type of lawyer whose traditional role is to offer legal services to clients apart from acting as their advocate in court. A solicitor instructs barristers to act as an advocate for their client in court, although rights of audience for solicitors vary according to jurisdiction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dde421b8-83a0-36dd-bd0e-6972cbe7457b",
                                        "entry_id": "7012547b-5700-3c3c-929b-7175e01cf81e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In English Canada and in parts of Australia, a type of lawyer who historically held the same role as above, but whose role has in modern times been merged with that of a barrister."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aed34b20-47f9-39bc-a0ff-37a2c9e5b281",
                                        "entry_id": "7012547b-5700-3c3c-929b-7175e01cf81e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In parts of the U.S., the chief legal officer of a city, town or other jurisdiction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb52729a-5809-39b3-b35e-6a93b3a66538",
                                        "entry_id": "7012547b-5700-3c3c-929b-7175e01cf81e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person soliciting sales, especially door to door."
                                        ],
